WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.627
It's difficult to imagine

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:03.170
anyone other
than Penn Badgley

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:06.173
playing the notorious
Joe Goldberg from YOU.

00:00:06.256 --> 00:00:08.675
Hello... you.

00:00:08.759 --> 00:00:10.636
His ability to switch
from a normal guy

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:14.848
to an unhinged serial killer
in the space of seconds

00:00:14.932 --> 00:00:17.518
makes YOU the stellar hit
it has become.

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:18.810
Before he was Joe,

00:00:18.894 --> 00:00:21.146
you may have known him
as Todd from Easy A

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.024
or perhaps Dan Humphrey
from Gossip Girl.

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:25.901
In honour of YOU season 3,

00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:28.320
let's take a look at how
Penn Badgley arrived here

00:00:28.403 --> 00:00:30.364
on his Road To Netflix.

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:32.282
Some of the most
striking parts of YOU

00:00:32.366 --> 00:00:35.244
are, of course,
Joe Goldberg's narration...

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.955
I still believe in the one.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.414
...so it may not
surprise you to hear

00:00:39.498 --> 00:00:41.208
that Penn's
earlier acting work

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:42.584
was in voiceovers.

00:00:42.668 --> 00:00:43.669
Believe it or not,

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:45.754
his first credits
were for voice work

00:00:45.838 --> 00:00:47.965
in the video games
Mario Golf 64

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:51.510
and Mario Tennis 64
in 1999 and 2000,

00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:52.719
doing all the tennis

00:00:52.803 --> 00:00:54.638
and golf-playing
sound effects.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.099
His early TV credits
included bit parts

00:00:57.182 --> 00:00:58.767
on various shows
and sitcoms,

00:00:58.851 --> 00:01:01.144
like this small part
playing a bully

00:01:01.228 --> 00:01:03.063
on hit sitcom
Will &amp; Grace...

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:05.732
-Can put your make-up in it.
-Hey, hey, hey!

00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:07.484
Give him his backpack.

00:01:07.568 --> 00:01:10.696
...and in 2002, here he is
alongside Amanda Bynes

00:01:10.779 --> 00:01:12.197
in What I Like About You...

00:01:12.823 --> 00:01:14.950
I think I actually saw
a flash of light!

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.827
That same year
he played the main role

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.162
of a 34-year-old
sent back in time

00:01:19.246 --> 00:01:21.999
to re-live his childhood
in Do Over

00:01:22.833 --> 00:01:23.876
Of all the times
to come back to,

00:01:23.959 --> 00:01:25.169
why this one?

00:01:25.252 --> 00:01:26.712
Tomorrow was the worst day
of my life!

00:01:26.795 --> 00:01:28.547
Penn played
the 14-year-old version

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.799
of Jake,
blessed with adult wisdom

00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:32.301
and a chance
to re-do the things

00:01:32.384 --> 00:01:34.178
that went wrong for him
as a teen.

00:01:34.261 --> 00:01:36.513
He went on to star
in more series

00:01:36.597 --> 00:01:39.892
like The Mountain,
a drama set at a ski resort,

00:01:39.975 --> 00:01:42.311
and 2006's
The Bedford Diaries,

00:01:42.394 --> 00:01:44.646
where he starred
as college freshman, Owen.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.648
That same year,
he had his movie debut

00:01:46.732 --> 00:01:48.817
in the now
classic teen romcom

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.360
John Tucker Must Die,

00:01:50.444 --> 00:01:51.695
he played
the younger brother

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.238
of the titular John Tucker,

00:01:53.322 --> 00:01:55.991
a popular jock
dating three girls at once.

00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:57.367
His character
becomes friends

00:01:57.451 --> 00:01:58.660
with the girl they recruit

00:01:58.744 --> 00:02:00.913
to try and ruin
the basketball star's life.

00:02:00.996 --> 00:02:02.664
He will say
that it was my fault,

00:02:02.748 --> 00:02:04.124
but I clearly said,

00:02:04.708 --> 00:02:06.835
"Dear God, man,
you're on fire."

00:02:06.919 --> 00:02:08.170
"Run for your life,"

00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:09.546
On to 2007

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:12.299
and to one of Penn's
best known roles,

00:02:12.382 --> 00:02:14.885
the one and only
Dan Humphrey in Gossip Girl.

00:02:15.552 --> 00:02:17.554
Trash? Look, man,
I live in Brooklyn.

00:02:17.638 --> 00:02:19.306
All right? Not the Ozarks.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.141
No offence to the Ozarks.

00:02:21.225 --> 00:02:24.061
It was actually a part
he initially turned down,

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:26.104
but took on after producers
struggled to find

00:02:26.188 --> 00:02:27.314
anyone else suitable.

00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:28.649
And it's just as well.

00:02:28.732 --> 00:02:31.151
The role helped catapult
his career and earned him

00:02:31.235 --> 00:02:33.445
16 Choice Awards
nominations.

00:02:33.529 --> 00:02:35.364
If you somehow
haven't seen it,

00:02:35.447 --> 00:02:36.490
the show follows the lives

00:02:36.573 --> 00:02:37.991
of uber-rich kids
in Manhattan

00:02:38.075 --> 00:02:40.994
who are closely watched
by a mysterious blogger

00:02:41.078 --> 00:02:43.080
known only as gossip girl.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.249
The show became a huge hit

00:02:45.332 --> 00:02:47.209
and had a massive
cultural impact,

00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:49.545
turning its stars
into huge celebrities

00:02:49.628 --> 00:02:51.296
over the course
of its six seasons.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.173
Penn's Dan,
a fish out of water

00:02:53.257 --> 00:02:54.466
as the only Brooklynite

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.343
among
his super-rich classmates

00:02:56.426 --> 00:02:59.221
was central to the story
as the so-called lonely boy

00:02:59.304 --> 00:03:00.264
who moons over,

00:03:00.347 --> 00:03:02.057
and eventually
gets a chance with,

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.476
Blake Lively's
Serena van der Woodsen.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.478
Several chances, actually.

00:03:06.562 --> 00:03:08.272
True, I may have peeked.

00:03:08.355 --> 00:03:09.690
By the end
of the six seasons,

00:03:09.773 --> 00:03:10.607
spoiler alert,

00:03:10.691 --> 00:03:13.735
we find out Dan
was in fact gossip girl

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:15.112
all along.

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:17.239
You're no one
until you talk to them.

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.951
So, you came home,
told all of this to Jenny,

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.036
and that was the beginning
of gossip girl?

00:03:23.871 --> 00:03:26.498
Could there be some echoes
of Joe Goldberg there?

00:03:26.582 --> 00:03:28.959
Who could forget
2010's Easy A

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:31.420
in which Emma Stone
played Olive Pendergast,

00:03:31.503 --> 00:03:32.671
a teen who tries to use

00:03:32.754 --> 00:03:34.590
her school's
active rumour mill

00:03:34.673 --> 00:03:37.092
in her favour,
with mixed results.

00:03:37.176 --> 00:03:39.678
Penn starred as Olive's
love interest, Todd.

00:03:39.761 --> 00:03:41.930
I, uh, I borrowed
my neighbour's mower

00:03:42.014 --> 00:03:42.848
I came right over.

00:03:42.931 --> 00:03:44.850
-That almost rhymed.
-I know.

00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:46.310
I spent a minute on it.

00:03:46.393 --> 00:03:47.728
He also, at one point,

00:03:47.811 --> 00:03:49.396
appears
wearing a beaver costume.

00:03:56.904 --> 00:03:58.697
In 2011's Margin Call,

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.073
Penn joined
an ensemble cast,

00:04:00.157 --> 00:04:02.826
including Zachary Quinto
and Stanley Tucci,

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:04.244
a film based loosely

00:04:04.328 --> 00:04:06.830
on the early stages
of the financial crash.

00:04:06.914 --> 00:04:07.748
Fuck me!

00:04:07.831 --> 00:04:09.541
Once this thing gets going
in the wrong direction

00:04:09.625 --> 00:04:12.920
this is...
this is fucking huge.

00:04:13.504 --> 00:04:15.756
Penn plays Seth,
a junior analyst

00:04:15.839 --> 00:04:17.591
dragged into
a growing scandal

00:04:17.674 --> 00:04:19.551
at a Wall Street
investment bank.

00:04:19.635 --> 00:04:20.594
The following year,

00:04:20.677 --> 00:04:22.763
he took on the role
of musician Jeff Buckley,

00:04:22.846 --> 00:04:24.723
in
Greetings from Tim Buckley,

00:04:24.806 --> 00:04:26.558
a film exploring
Buckley's relationship

00:04:26.642 --> 00:04:28.185
with his father's legacy,

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:29.561
culminating with a concert

00:04:29.645 --> 00:04:31.271
where he performed
his songs.

00:04:31.813 --> 00:04:34.942
It's like all these people
playing tribute to Tim.

00:04:35.025 --> 00:04:35.901
He spent his entire life

00:04:35.984 --> 00:04:37.277
abandoning
the people we love,

00:04:37.361 --> 00:04:38.904
so, like,
what am I doing here?

00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:40.531
With that performance
in mind,

00:04:40.614 --> 00:04:41.657
it's probably
no surprise to hear

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:43.283
Penn also has
a music career,

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:45.911
fronting four-piece
Indie pop band MOTHXR.

00:04:45.994 --> 00:04:49.039
He and three of his friends
formed the band in 2013,

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:50.249
recording
their first five songs

00:04:50.332 --> 00:04:52.918
in a bungalow in LA
over eight days.

00:04:53.001 --> 00:04:55.546
They released
their debut album Centerfold

00:04:55.629 --> 00:04:57.047
in 2016.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.424
That brings us to 2018

00:04:59.508 --> 00:05:02.344
and Penn's latest
and most terrifying role.

00:05:02.427 --> 00:05:05.264
-And you're Joe...
-Goldberg.

00:05:05.347 --> 00:05:07.307
On the face of it,
he's a mild-mannered

00:05:07.391 --> 00:05:08.851
and charming
book store manager.

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:11.520
In reality, he's a stalker
and a serial killer,

00:05:11.603 --> 00:05:13.522
twisting the tropes
of romantic films

00:05:13.605 --> 00:05:16.275
to fit his unhinged
behaviour towards women.

00:05:16.358 --> 00:05:17.901
When he meets
Guinevere Beck,

00:05:17.985 --> 00:05:20.737
he slowly insinuates himself
into her life,

00:05:20.821 --> 00:05:23.198
stealing her phone,
stalking her around campus

00:05:23.282 --> 00:05:25.492
and killing
her sort of boyfriend.

00:05:25.576 --> 00:05:27.536
I would do anything for you.

00:05:29.496 --> 00:05:30.789
How many guys are willing
to do anything

00:05:30.873 --> 00:05:31.790
for the person they love?

00:05:31.874 --> 00:05:33.083
Honestly, Beck,
you're lucky to have me.

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:36.086
This was another role
he almost didn't take on,

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:37.963
worrying
about the nature of it.

00:05:38.046 --> 00:05:38.964
But, in the end,

00:05:39.047 --> 00:05:40.215
he was convinced
by the script

00:05:40.299 --> 00:05:42.593
and the social commentary
the series would provide.

00:05:42.676 --> 00:05:44.636
Then, there's the link
between this role

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:46.013
and the other
he's best known for.

00:05:46.096 --> 00:05:48.182
Dan Humphrey
literally wrote himself

00:05:48.265 --> 00:05:49.766
into Serena's life

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:51.685
and viewers have definitely
seen the connection

00:05:51.768 --> 00:05:52.811
between the two.

00:05:52.895 --> 00:05:54.563
Penn himself seems to agree,

00:05:54.646 --> 00:05:56.940
telling the New Yorker:
"It's the same role,

00:05:57.024 --> 00:05:59.526
it's just Joe has blood
dripping down his face."

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.695
He's also been very quick
to remind people

00:06:01.778 --> 00:06:02.988
thirsting over Joe Goldberg

00:06:03.071 --> 00:06:05.574
that this guy
is a literal serial killer.

00:06:07.451 --> 00:06:10.120
YOU became a worldwide hit
after it dropped on Netflix,

00:06:10.204 --> 00:06:11.830
returning
for two more seasons.

00:06:11.914 --> 00:06:12.956
In the latest,

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:14.374
Joe is a father in suburbia

00:06:14.458 --> 00:06:16.919
with his equally
unhinged wife, Love.

00:06:17.002 --> 00:06:19.296
I think we need to go
to couple's therapy.

00:06:21.089 --> 00:06:22.633
But to find out
what happens there,

00:06:22.716 --> 00:06:23.967
you'll have to catch
series 3

00:06:24.051 --> 00:06:25.719
now streaming on Netflix.

